### Connect 

To check whether a connected account has enabled MobilePay, inspect `capabilities.mobilepay_payments` in the [Accounts API or webhooks](https://docs.stripe.com/api/accounts/object.md#account_object-capabilities-mobilepay_payments) and confirm that it’s `active`. For connected accounts without full Stripe Dashboard access, request the `mobilepay_payments` capability using the [Capabilities API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/capabilities.md). Learn more about [enabling payment methods for connected accounts](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/account-capabilities.md).

## 3D Secure authentication

Certain cards or banks might require an additional *card authentication* (A bank might require the customer to authenticate a card payment before processing. Implementation varies by bank but commonly consists of a customer entering in a security code sent to their phone) step to process a MobilePay transaction. When this occurs, the MobilePay app presents a WebView that prompts the customer to authorize the payment. The *3D Secure challenge* (3D Secure (3DS) provides an additional layer of authentication for credit card transactions that protects businesses from liability for fraudulent card payments) is invisible to your integration, and you don’t need to handle additional integration steps.

### Liability shift

[Liability shift](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/3d-secure/authentication-flow.md#disputed-payments) applies to a MobilePay payment only when *3D Secure authentication* (3D Secure (3DS) provides an additional layer of authentication for credit card transactions that protects businesses from liability for fraudulent card payments) occurred. You can’t force 3D Secure authentication on the underlying card payment.

## Current limitations 

### Dankort support

Stripe doesn’t process these payments over the Dankort network. For co-branded Visa/Dankort cards, Stripe uses Visa.

## Fees 

Because MobilePay payments use underlying card transactions, you pay Stripe’s standard card-processing fees and applicable taxes. Stripe deducts those amounts from each successful transaction.

The MobilePay transaction surcharge isn’t deducted from the individual payment. Stripe aggregates these surcharges, bills them daily, and deducts the amount from your [Stripe balance](https://dashboard.stripe.com/balance).

Applicable Danish merchants of record also pay a monthly MobilePay membership fee while active. See [Pricing](https://stripe.com/pricing) for fee details. Stripe bills the fee monthly and deducts it from your Stripe balance. Automatic inactivity offboarding can stop the membership fee, and negotiated or platform-specific arrangements can differ.

MobilePay fees appear as a separate entry on your monthly tax invoice. You can find monthly invoices in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/documents).

## Branding 

Your customer’s MobilePay app displays the icon configured in your [Branding settings](https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/branding.md). If you haven’t configured an icon, the app displays a default icon instead.

## Customer experience 

#### 1. Choose MobilePay

Select MobilePay at checkout.

#### 2. Continue to MobilePay

On desktop, continue to MobilePay's payment page and enter the phone number linked to your MobilePay account. On mobile, continue to the MobilePay app.

#### 3. Approve the payment

On desktop, open the notification and approve in MobilePay. On mobile, review the payment in the app and select a card. Choose another card if needed, and complete additional issuer authentication if prompted.

#### 4. Return to the business

Return to the business's website or app to view the payment result. Returning doesn't by itself prove that the payment succeeded.

### Card transaction retries 

MobilePay lets customers retry a card payment in the app before the payment reaches a terminal failure. If a card transaction fails, the customer can choose another card and retry the payment.

### Statement descriptors 

MobilePay payments use the standard card statement-descriptor path. For card payments, use `statement_descriptor_suffix` to combine your account’s shortened descriptor with a payment-specific suffix. Setting the full `statement_descriptor` follows separate full-descriptor and legacy fallback behavior and doesn’t append in the same way as a suffix. The complete card descriptor can contain up to 22 characters, and issuers can truncate, reformat, or display merchant information differently.

For Connect direct charges, Stripe uses the connected account’s descriptor. For destination charges, Stripe uses the platform’s descriptor unless you set `on_behalf_of`, in which case Stripe uses the connected account’s descriptor. Learn more about [statement descriptors](https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/statement-descriptors.md) and [statement descriptors with Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/statement-descriptors.md).

## Enable MobilePay 

If you use Stripe front-end products, enable MobilePay in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe automatically determines which payment methods are most relevant to each customer.

If your integration lists payment methods manually, learn how to [configure MobilePay as a payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/mobilepay/accept-a-payment.md).
